  "register": "hyderabad",
  "description": "The signature Hyderabadi flavor words — hau, nakko, kaiku, are, endi ra — and how they map to standard Telugu.",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "u49-i01",
      "te": "హౌ, వస్తున్నా.",
      "gloss": "Yes, I'm coming.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "హౌ", "gloss": "yes (Hyderabadi)" },
        { "te": "వస్తున్నా", "gloss": "I'm coming" }
      ],
      "tags": ["flavor", "yes-no"],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "note": "హౌ (hau) is the Hyderabadi 'yes', borrowed from Dakhni Urdu. Standard Telugu: అవును. You'll hear హౌ everywhere in the city.",
      "distractors": ["u49-i02", "u49-i09"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u49-i02",
      "te": "నక్కో అన్నా, నక్కో.",
      "gloss": "No anna, no.",
      "words": [
        { "te": "నక్కో", "gloss": "no / don't want (Hyderabadi)" },
        { "te": "అన్నా", "gloss": "anna (brother)" },
        { "te": "నక్కో", "gloss": "no / don't want (Hyderabadi)" }
      ],
      "tags": ["flavor", "yes-no"],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "note": "నక్కో (nakko) is the Dakhni 'no / don't' — standard Telugu వద్దు. Doubling it (నక్కో నక్కో) makes the refusal friendly but firm.",
      "distractors": ["u49-i01", "u49-i10"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u49-i03",
      "te": "కైకు రా ఇంత టెన్షన్?",
      "gloss": "Why so much tension, ra?",
      "words": [
        { "te": "కైకు", "gloss": "why (Hyderabadi)" },
        { "te": "రా", "gloss": "ra (casual particle)" },
        { "te": "ఇంత", "gloss": "this much" },
        { "te": "టెన్షన్", "gloss": "tension / worry" }
      ],
      "tags": ["flavor", "questions"],
      "difficulty": 3,
      "note": "కైకు (kaiku) = 'why', straight from Dakhni Urdu. Standard Telugu: ఎందుకు. A very Hyderabadi way to tell someone to relax."
    },
    {
      "id": "u49-i04",
      "te": "అరే, ఇటు రా!",
      "gloss": "Hey, come this way!",
      "words": [
        { "te": "అరే", "gloss": "hey!" },
        { "te": "ఇటు", "gloss": "this way" },
        { "te": "రా", "gloss": "come (casual)" }
      ],
      "tags": ["flavor", "commands"],
      "difficulty": 2,
      "note": "అరే / అరేయ్ is the all-purpose Hyderabadi attention-grabber — for friends only, never for elders. Standard Telugu might use ఏయ్ or just the name.",
      "distractors": ["u49-i05", "u49-i06"]
    },
    {
      "id": "u49-i05",
      "te": "అరేయ్, ఎక్కడున్నావ్ రా?",
